{"requirements":[{"id":"local-login-banner","requirement":"Display “Authorized access only” before local logins on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The agetty issue renderer displayed the exact required text before and after reboot, while the local getty services were active.","evidence_ids":["cmd-108bb711da0a4586","cmd-9e988d3dac3447c3","cmd-d5865946fa8349d2","cmd-76fb15a28c6a4dd3"]},{"id":"ssh-login-banner","requirement":"Display “Authorized access only” before SSH logins on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"sshd used /etc/issue.net, listened on port 22, and final live probes before and after reboot displayed the exact text before authentication denial. One earlier probe omitted the banner, but the later repeated observations establish the final behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5d41927249d40c8","cmd-867f9bb93c6a4d50","cmd-7dab7777515f45a2","cmd-53e4af884bfc4d22","cmd-d5865946fa8349d2","cmd-7d250c5fdbce47d8"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Writing the two banner files and SSH drop-in, generating required host keys, enabling sshd, reloading agetty, and performing the mandatory reboot all had clear task or evidence-protocol roles. Staging files were removed. After reboot there were no failed services, package-database errors, or unexpected temporary-file residue; the newly exposed SSH port was required and retained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05fa509a67634d29","cmd-521b41d092fd4606","cmd-1cdf6b79c7774f8c","cmd-867f9bb93c6a4d50","cmd-eec7291d25e84d5b","cmd-2d666ad14eb746b8","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both contractual outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is strong: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot scheduling and connection interruption, a changed boot ID, a running recovered system, restored services and configuration, and successful post-restart banner tests. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["One early SSH probe did not capture the banner, despite later pre-reboot and post-reboot probes succeeding with otherwise equivalent options (cmd-7dab7777515f45a2).","Local behavior was tested using agetty’s issue renderer in a pseudo-terminal rather than by capturing the already-running tty1 or ttyS0 login prompt directly; active getty services and the successful post-reboot rendering provide strong corroboration."]}
